All 7 diff-engine tests pass. Now let me add an end-to-end FFI test (offscreen) that proves Rust→C++ command batch marshalling + string crossing + apply_count. Let me add it to ffi.rs or a test module. It needs the Qt offscreen env set before init. Since QGuiApplication is process-global, and only one test creates it, I'll put it as a single #[test] in a separate module. But there's a risk: cargo runs tests in parallel; the Qt test must not conflict with other tests (they don't touch Qt). Only ONE test uses Qt. OK.

Also: QGuiApplication can only be created once per process. If the test binary also runs other Qt tests, conflict. I'll add just one.

Let me add the FFI round-trip test in ffi.rs:

```rust
#[cfg(test)]
mod tests {
    use super::*;

    #[test]
    fn command_batch_crosses_into_cpp_offscreen() {
        std::env::set_var("QT_QPA_PLATFORM", "offscreen");
        std::env::set_var("QT_QUICK_BACKEND", "software");
        unsafe {
            assert_eq!(pathland_qt_layer_init(noop_wake, noop_tick, std::ptr::null_mut()), 0);
            let text = "hello";
            let cmds = [
                Command::create_node(1, 0x10),
                Command::insert_child(0, 1, u32::MAX),
                Command::set_text(1, text),
            ];
            pathland_qt_layer_apply(cmds.as_ptr(), cmds.len() as u32);
            assert_eq!(pathland_qt_layer_apply_count(), 3);
            let mut buf = [0i8; 64];
            let n = pathland_qt_layer_last_text(buf.as_mut_ptr(), buf.len() as u32);
            assert_eq!(n, text.len() as u32);
            let got = std::ffi::CStr::from_ptr(buf.as_ptr()).to_string_lossy();
            assert_eq!(got, text);
            pathland_qt_layer_shutdown();
        }
    }
    extern "C" fn noop_wake(_user: *mut std::ffi::c_void) {}
    extern "C" fn noop_tick(_user: *mut std::ffi::c_void) {}
}
```

Wait — the Command struct in ffi.rs is `#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy)]` with `str_: *const c_char`. The test's `text` local is a &str; Command::set_text borrows it. The Vec/array of Commands holds pointers to `text` — valid during the apply call. Good.

But `Command::create_node` returns Command with `str_` null — Copy fine.

Let me add this test to ffi.rs. Also need `Command` builders accessible in ffi tests (they're in the same module — yes).

One concern: `pathland_qt_layer_init` creates QGuiApplication. On macOS, the "QApplication was not created in the main() thread" warning appears but works offscreen (as the spike showed). Fine.

